{
  "raw": {
    "https://furman.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/Furman_Careers/job/Main-Campus/Writer---Media-Relations-Specialist_R003380": {
      "title": "Writer & Media Relations Specialist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-03\nFull time\n\nWelcome to Furman University's Career Site! IMPORTANT :​ Load all documents in the My Experience area under Resume/CV . This may include your resume/C.V., cover letter, unofficial transcript, teaching philosophy, etc. Please wait for all documents to finish uploading before clicking Next. If the process times out you will lose your progress, so please ensure you have all necessary documents available before starting. The drop-down lists only display so many options: please type into a drop-down list to search for your option. For example: in Field of Study, you may need to enter your field name. If you have no field, type \"None.\" If you have previously applied, make sure your information is current as you can transfer it to another application. Prior to submitting your application, verify all information for accuracy and ensure you have uploaded all appropriate documents.  Once submitted, you will not be able to edit your application other than to change your contact information. If you have any questions or need additional assistance, please contact the Office of Human Resources via email at recruitment@furman.edu  or by calling 864-294-3103. Job Title: Writer & Media Relations Specialist Job Family: Professionals Full-Time/Part-Time: Full time Pay Type: Salary Department: Strategic Communications Job Summary: As a member of University Marketing & Communications at Furman University, the Writer & Media Relations Specialist is responsible for writing and editing news content, feature stories and copy across multiple mediums, and for proactive and responsive Media Relations with the goal of illustrating the impact of Furman University and its students, faculty, staff, alumni, donors and the broader community. The Writer & Media Relations Specialist creates and edits content for a wide range of print and digital communications, including magazine stories, news releases, marketing and advertising materials, web and social content, internal communications and presentations — adapting tone, format and length to fit the platform and the audience, from a long-form magazine feature to a short-form social caption built for the scroll. The Writer & Media Relations Specialist reports to the Director of Content Strategy and partners with departmental leadership, faculty and staff of the university in developing story ideas and editorial strategy. In addition to storytelling, the Writer & Media Relations Specialist provides daily media relations support under the direction of the Vice President and Assistant Vice President for University Communications — serving as a steady, trusted voice for Furman with reporters and media outlets, and helping protect and build the university’s reputation with both internal and external audiences. The Writer & Media Relations Specialist collaborates with all members of the University Marketing & Communications team, and with Furman faculty and staff, to deliver creative, accurate and compelling stories. The Writer & Media Relations Specialist is a proven expert in Associated Press style, feature writing and news writing, with the versatility to write well for any channel Furman’s story needs to reach. Job Description: Responsibilities Storytelling & Content Creation Write and edit news content, feature stories, profiles and institutional narratives that illustrate the impact of Furman University and its people. Create and edit copy for a wide range of print and digital communications, including magazine stories, news releases, marketing and advertising materials, internal communications and executive presentations. Interview faculty, staff, students, alumni and donors to source original, accurate and compelling stories. Apply Associated Press style consistently, along with Furman’s house style and editorial standards, across all written content. Media Relations & Reputation Provide daily media relations support on behalf of the university, under the direction of the Assistant Vice President for University Communications — including responding to reporter inquiries, coordinating interview requests and drafting statements and talking points. Serve as a trusted, front-line point of contact for media, representing Furman with professionalism, accuracy and care in every interaction. Monitor daily news and media coverage of Furman, proactively flagging emerging stories, risks and opportunities to the Assistant Vice President and Director of Content Strategy. Help shape and protect Furman’s reputation with both internal audiences (faculty, staff, students) and external audiences (media, prospective students, alumni, donors and the broader public), ensuring consistent, accurate messaging across every touchpoint. Support the university’s response to sensitive or time-sensitive situations by drafting clear, accurate communications quickly, escalating appropriately to the Assistant Vice President. Multi-Channel & Digital Adaptation Adapt stories and messaging across mediums — print, web, social, video scripts and advertising — tailoring tone, length and format to fit each platform and audience. Write and edit web and social copy with an understanding of how content is discovered and consumed online, including search visibility (SEO/AEO/GEO) and platform-specific best practices for social and digital engagement. Draft scripts and copy for video, podcast and other emerging storytelling formats as Furman’s communications channels evolve. Use available data and performance insights — in partnership with digital and marketing colleagues — to inform how stories are framed, formatted and distributed across channels. Editorial Collaboration & Strategy Partner with the Director of Content Strategy and UMC leadership to develop story ideas, editorial calendars and content strategy that align with institutional priorities. Collaborate with colleagues across University Marketing & Communications — including design, digital strategy and social media — to ensure stories are told cohesively across every channel. Work closely with Furman faculty, staff and campus partners to identify newsworthy stories and ensure accuracy and appropriate context in coverage. Contribute to brainstorming and planning for major institutional storytelling initiatives, campaigns and special publications. Brand Voice & Editorial Standards Adapt the tone of writing to ensure messages are effectively targeted toward specific audiences — prospective students, alumni, donors, faculty/staff or the broader public — while maintaining a consistent institutional voice. Serve as a steward of Furman’s editorial voice and style standards, helping ensure consistency across contributors and channels. Fact-check and proofread content to ensure accuracy, clarity and adherence to AP and Furman house style. Professional Practice Manage multiple writing assignments and deadlines simultaneously in a fast-paced, deadline-driven environment. Use generative AI tools responsibly and selectively — for research support, brainstorming or first-draft acceleration — while ensuring all published work reflects original reporting, editorial judgment and Furman’s authentic voice. Stay current on trends in journalism, digital storytelling and higher education communications, bringing fresh ideas back to the team. Perform other duties as assigned. Experience and Required Skills Bachelor’s degree in journalism, English, communications or a related field. 5 or more years of professional writing and editing experience, preferably in journalism, higher education communications or content marketing. Proven expertise in Associated Press style, feature writing and news writing. Experience providing media relations support — responding to reporter inquiries, drafting statements and talking points, and representing an organization’s voice accurately and calmly under deadline pressure. Demonstrated ability to write effectively across multiple formats and platforms — print, web, social, video scripts and advertising copy. Working understanding of how content performs across digital and social platforms, and comfort adapting long-form writing for short-form, platform-native consumption. Familiarity with generative AI tools and their appropriate, responsible use in a writing and editorial workflow. Excellent interviewing skills and the ability to build trust quickly with faculty, staff, students, alumni and donors. Strong collaborative instincts, with the ability to take and give constructive feedback across a team of writers, editors and designers. Exceptional attention to detail, with strong fact-checking and proofreading skills. Ability to manage multiple deadlines and shifting priorities in a fast-paced newsroom-style environment. Work Conditions Work is performed under usual office conditions. University Marketing & Communications Culture and Values Statement University Marketing & Communications’ values are grounded in professionalism, respect and humility. We are unified, driven and purposeful in pursuing our common goal of advancing Furman University. We approach every task as problem-solvers who are curious, creative and innovative — and good listeners first. We value each other’s talents, and understand that achieving excellence requires care and attention to the personal growth and well-being of each member of our team. At the end of the day, our work should be fun, engaging and inspiring — and create advocates across the Furman community and beyond. Application Requirements Resume Cover letter Writing samples (a mix of long-form and short-form/digital work is preferred) These should be attached as a single PDF Candidates selected for interviews will be expected to discuss their editorial process, experience adapting stories across platforms, and examples of storytelling that required close collaboration with subjects or campus partners. Education Requirements: Bachelors Certification Requirements: Job Posting End Date (if date is blank, posting is open ended):"
    },
    "https://furman.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/Furman_Careers/job/Main-Campus/Deputy-General-Counsel_R003350": {
      "title": "Deputy General Counsel",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-27\nFull time\n\nWelcome to Furman University's Career Site! IMPORTANT :​ Load all documents in the My Experience area under Resume/CV . This may include your resume/C.V., cover letter, unofficial transcript, teaching philosophy, etc. Please wait for all documents to finish uploading before clicking Next. If the process times out you will lose your progress, so please ensure you have all necessary documents available before starting. The drop-down lists only display so many options: please type into a drop-down list to search for your option. For example: in Field of Study, you may need to enter your field name. If you have no field, type \"None.\" If you have previously applied, make sure your information is current as you can transfer it to another application. Prior to submitting your application, verify all information for accuracy and ensure you have uploaded all appropriate documents.  Once submitted, you will not be able to edit your application other than to change your contact information. If you have any questions or need additional assistance, please contact the Office of Human Resources via email at recruitment@furman.edu  or by calling 864-294-3103. Job Title: Deputy General Counsel Job Family: Professionals Full-Time/Part-Time: Full time Pay Type: Salary Department: General Counsel Job Summary: The Deputy General Counsel will be a senior member of the Office of General Counsel and will serve as a key advisor to the Vice President and General Counsel. The successful candidate must be able to manage a demanding and wide-ranging practice, exercise sound legal and practical judgment, and communicate effectively with colleagues and clients. The candidate will be expected to handle significant and complex matters and transactions from beginning to end with minimal supervision. Job Description: JOB DESCRIPTION Principal Duties and Responsibilities Provide timely legal advice to university divisions on day-to-day matters pertaining to the operation of the university, including in particular those related to staff employment, tort liability, student issues, athletics, research and sponsored programs, and data privacy and security. Review, draft, and negotiate contracts on behalf of the University. Develop and maintain legal templates, forms, and guidance documents. Assist policy makers in drafting, revising, and implementing institutional policies and procedures and provide advice regarding the legal implications of institutional policies and initiatives. Coordinate litigation and other significant legal matters in consultation with the Vice President and General Counsel; gather information and manage discovery for litigation and administrative investigations. Manage responses to subpoenas, document requests, records inquiries, and data privacy requests in coordination with relevant offices. Conduct legal research and provide advice on legal and regulatory issues affecting the university. Provide guidance and support to other members of the Office of General Counsel, as appropriate, and contribute to the effective administration and operation of the office. Serve as the Vice President and General Counsel’s designee on University committees, working groups, and other institutional matters, as appropriate. In the absence of the Vice President and General Counsel, exercise such authority and responsibility as may be delegated by the Vice President and General Counsel. Maintain strong relationships across the University to provide accessible, solutions-oriented counsel that supports Furman’s mission and priorities. Work on special projects in response to needs as assigned by the General Counsel and perform duties as required and/or assigned by the VPGC. Qualifications Juris Doctor (J.D.) degree from an American Bar Association-accredited law school. Licensed to practice law in the State of South Carolina, or eligible for licensure within a reasonable time from the date of hire. A minimum of 5 years of recent experience as a practicing attorney, with substantial proficiency and depth in one or more of the following areas: drafting and negotiating sophisticated agreements, civil litigation, employment, research and sponsored programs, Division 1 college athletics, and/or privacy laws. A solid working knowledge of the legal, academic, and operational issues relevant to the operations of a liberal arts institution, with willingness to develop new subject matter expertise as client needs dictate . Experience in a college or university general counsel’s office is strongly preferred. Strong research and analytical skills, coupled with sound judgment and the ability to balance legal risks with other priorities. Capacity to thrive in a collaborative, collegial environment and work independently with a high degree of motivation. Demonstrated ability to handle multiple, unrelated matters concurrently and to perform effectively under the pressure of frequent interruptions, conflicting demands, and changing priorities. Demonstrated ability to identify potential legal issues and the long-term implications of policy and legal decisions. Demonstrated ability to establish relationships with various constituencies; work collaboratively to find solutions to very complex problems; and to lead and participate in complex projects requiring a team approach for resolution. Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. High ethical standards, reflecting honesty, integrity, and reliability. Strong client service orientation and skills. Education Requirements: Juris Doctor (Required) Certification Requirements: Job Posting End Date (if date is blank, posting is open ended):"
    },
    "https://furman.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/Furman_Careers/job/Main-Campus/Professor-of-Biology---Invertebrate-Zoology-Entomology--Assistant-Associate-Full-_R003354": {
      "title": "Professor of Biology - Invertebrate Zoology/Entomology (Assistant/Associate/Full)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-27\nFull time\n\nWelcome to Furman University's Career Site! IMPORTANT :​ Load all documents in the My Experience area under Resume/CV . This may include your resume/C.V., cover letter, unofficial transcript, teaching philosophy, etc. Please wait for all documents to finish uploading before clicking Next. If the process times out you will lose your progress, so please ensure you have all necessary documents available before starting. The drop-down lists only display so many options: please type into a drop-down list to search for your option. For example: in Field of Study, you may need to enter your field name. If you have no field, type \"None.\" If you have previously applied, make sure your information is current as you can transfer it to another application. Prior to submitting your application, verify all information for accuracy and ensure you have uploaded all appropriate documents.  Once submitted, you will not be able to edit your application other than to change your contact information. If you have any questions or need additional assistance, please contact the Office of Human Resources via email at recruitment@furman.edu  or by calling 864-294-3103. Job Title: Professor of Biology - Invertebrate Zoology/Entomology (Assistant/Associate/Full) Job Family: Furman Faculty Full-Time/Part-Time: Full time Pay Type: Salary Department: Biology Job Summary: Furman University invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position in Biology at the rank of Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Full Professor, beginning August 2027. Job Description: We seek a broadly trained biologist who is excited to teach across the undergraduate curriculum, mentor students in authentic research, and contribute to a collaborative liberal arts and sciences community. Teaching expectations for this position may include lecture and laboratory courses from a newly revised slate of introductory biology and data science courses. We are interested in recruiting candidates with expertise in teaching entomology and/or other areas of invertebrate biology. Candidates with expertise in related areas are also encouraged to apply. Other teaching responsibilities may include opportunities to develop new upper-level courses in the candidate’s area of expertise, especially those that broaden our current course offerings. The Department of Biology currently has 15 full-time Biology faculty members and offers both a B.A. and a B.S. degree in Biology. Furman University is located in the Piedmont of Upstate South Carolina near the Blue Ridge Mountains, which provides a rich environment for local field classes and research. In addition, the Department of Biology offers study away programs in Belize, Ecuador, New Mexico, and South Africa. The area of research specialization for this position is flexible, and we welcome applicants whose scholarship complements and extends the department’s current strengths. The successful candidate will be expected to establish and sustain a rigorous scholarly program that produces peer-reviewed work. Faculty in the Department of Biology are expected to engage with undergraduate students as collaborators in their scholarly work, which frequently involves summer research activities. Furman offers competitive start-up funds, individual research space, and institutional financial support for faculty-mentored undergraduate research and student conference participation. The Department of Biology is housed with other sciences in the 200,000 square-foot Charles H. Townes Science Center. Faculty members have access to shared instrumentation that supports a broad range of research activities including microscopy (confocal, SEM), mammalian tissue-culture, molecular biology instrumentation (including thermal cyclers, qPCR system, DNA sequence analyzer, microplate readers for absorbance- and fluorescence-based spectrophotometry and digital gel and blot imaging systems), and an NIH-compliant animal facility. The Department of Biology also houses a BodyViz system (a 3D anatomy learning platform based on real patient CT and MRI data that allows students to virtually dissect hundreds of vertebrate bodies including humans and other animals) and several natural history collections (including a herbarium, a vertebrate collection, and an insect collection). For further information on our department, please visit https://www.furman.edu/academics/biology/ . Biologists whose work integrates views from multiple areas of biology and other science disciplines are particularly encouraged to apply. The strongest candidates will demonstrate an understanding of – and enthusiasm for – teaching and conducting research at a primarily undergraduate liberal arts institution, providing students with a rich and varied educational experience, and enhancing inclusion in STEM. Candidates must hold a Ph.D. in Biology (or a related discipline) by August 1, 2027; ABD candidates will be considered, provided that the degree is conferred by that date. Prior university-level teaching experience and postdoctoral experience are highly preferred but not required. Furman University is dedicated to fostering a vibrant and inclusive community through excellence in teaching, mentorship, scholarship, and programming. We believe that cultural understanding, inclusiveness, and freedom of inquiry, thought, and discourse are essential components of a transformative undergraduate education. We advance these ideals with a liberal arts and sciences curriculum built on a substantial general education program, featuring traditional and innovative elements, and a robust portfolio of disciplinary and interdisciplinary major and minor areas of study. Additionally, we have established and continue to develop various initiatives, including historic projects, dialogue programs such as On Discourse and the Intergroup Dialogues Program, the Center for Interpersonal Connections, and four distinctive external-facing institutes. The successful candidate will have the ability to work with students from diverse backgrounds and contribute to Furman’s commitment to expanding access and opportunity to Furman’s rich learning culture. Applicants should submit the following documents as a single PDF in the order listed: a cover letter describing your qualifications and identifying the position for which you are applying (2 pages max), a curriculum vitae, a statement of teaching philosophy (2 pages max), a statement of research priorities outlining your plan to mentor undergraduates in research activities (3 pages max), unofficial undergraduate and graduate transcripts, and complete contact information for three references. The statement of teaching philosophy should describe your inclusive teaching and mentoring efforts, broadly conceived, and how your teaching and mentoring may contribute to a liberal arts and sciences community that aims, among other things, to “honor inquiry, promote diversity, [and] strive for equity” ( FUture Focused ). You may also discuss any relevant professional development, service contributions, or other experiences that have refined your skills, or demonstrate your efforts in these areas.   Review of applications will begin on October 5, 2026, and continue until the positions are filled.  Questions about this position may be directed to Dennis Haney, Professor of Biology (dennis.haney @furman.edu ) . Education Requirements: Certification Requirements: Job Posting End Date (if date is blank, posting is open ended):"
    },
    "https://furman.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/Furman_Careers/job/Main-Campus/Professor-of-Biology---Anatomy--Assistant-Associate-Full-_R003355": {
      "title": "Professor of Biology - Anatomy (Assistant/Associate/Full)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-27\nFull time\n\nWelcome to Furman University's Career Site! IMPORTANT :​ Load all documents in the My Experience area under Resume/CV . This may include your resume/C.V., cover letter, unofficial transcript, teaching philosophy, etc. Please wait for all documents to finish uploading before clicking Next. If the process times out you will lose your progress, so please ensure you have all necessary documents available before starting. The drop-down lists only display so many options: please type into a drop-down list to search for your option. For example: in Field of Study, you may need to enter your field name. If you have no field, type \"None.\" If you have previously applied, make sure your information is current as you can transfer it to another application. Prior to submitting your application, verify all information for accuracy and ensure you have uploaded all appropriate documents.  Once submitted, you will not be able to edit your application other than to change your contact information. If you have any questions or need additional assistance, please contact the Office of Human Resources via email at recruitment@furman.edu  or by calling 864-294-3103. Job Title: Professor of Biology - Anatomy (Assistant/Associate/Full) Job Family: Furman Faculty Full-Time/Part-Time: Full time Pay Type: Salary Department: Biology Job Summary: Furman University invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position in Biology at the rank of Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Full Professor, beginning August 2027. Job Description: We seek a broadly trained biologist who is excited to teach across the undergraduate curriculum, mentor students in authentic research, and contribute to a collaborative liberal arts and sciences community. Teaching expectations for this position may include lecture and laboratory courses from a newly revised slate of introductory biology and data science courses. We are interested in recruiting candidates with expertise in teaching human anatomy and/or comparative anatomy. Candidates with expertise in related areas are also encouraged to apply. Other teaching responsibilities may include opportunities to develop new upper-level courses in the candidate’s area of expertise, especially those that broaden our current course offerings. The Department of Biology currently has 15 full-time Biology faculty members and offers both a B.A. and a B.S. degree in Biology. Furman University is located in the Piedmont of Upstate South Carolina near the Blue Ridge Mountains , which provides a rich environment for local field classes and research. In addition, the Department of Biology offers study away programs in Belize, Ecuador, New Mexico, and South Africa.   The area of research specialization for this position is flexible, and we welcome applicants whose scholarship complements and extends the department’s current strengths. The successful candidate will be expected to establish and sustain a rigorous scholarly program that produces peer-reviewed work. Faculty in the Department of Biology are expected to engage with undergraduate students as collaborators in their scholarly work, which frequently involves summer research activities. Furman offers competitive start-up funds, individual research space, and institutional financial support for faculty-mentored undergraduate research and student conference participation. The Department of Biology is housed with other sciences in the 200,000 square-foot Charles H. Townes Science Center. Faculty members have access to shared instrumentation that supports a broad range of research activities including microscopy (confocal, SEM), mammalian tissue-culture, molecular biology instrumentation (including thermal cyclers, qPCR system, DNA sequence analyzer, microplate readers for absorbance- and fluorescence-based spectrophotometry and digital gel and blot imaging systems), and an NIH-compliant animal facility. The Department of Biology also houses a BodyViz system (a 3D anatomy learning platform based on real patient CT and MRI data that allows students to virtually dissect hundreds of vertebrate bodies including humans and other animals) and several natural history collections (including a herbarium, a vertebrate collection, and an insect collection). For further information on our department, please visit https://www.furman.edu/academics/biology/ .    Biologists whose work integrates views from multiple areas of biology and other science disciplines are particularly encouraged to apply. The strongest candidates will demonstrate an understanding of – and enthusiasm for – teaching and conducting research at a primarily undergraduate liberal arts institution, providing students with a rich and varied educational experience, and enhancing inclusion in STEM. Candidates must hold a Ph.D. in Biology (or a related discipline) by August 1, 2027; ABD candidates will be considered, provided that the degree is conferred by that date. Prior university-level teaching experience and postdoctoral experience are highly preferred but not required. Furman University is dedicated to fostering a vibrant and inclusive community through excellence in teaching, mentorship, scholarship, and programming. We believe that cultural understanding, inclusiveness, and freedom of inquiry, thought, and discourse are essential components of a transformative undergraduate education. We advance these ideals with a liberal arts and sciences curriculum built on a substantial general education program, featuring traditional and innovative elements, and a robust portfolio of disciplinary and interdisciplinary major and minor areas of study. Additionally, we have established and continue to develop various initiatives, including historic projects, dialogue programs such as On Discourse and the Intergroup Dialogues Program, the Center for Interpersonal Connections, and four distinctive external-facing institutes. The successful candidate will have the ability to work with students from diverse backgrounds and contribute to Furman’s commitment to expanding access and opportunity to Furman’s rich learning culture. Applicants should submit the following documents as a single PDF in the order listed: a cover letter describing your qualifications and identifying the position for which you are applying (2 pages max), a curriculum vitae, a statement of teaching philosophy (2 pages max), a statement of research priorities outlining your plan to mentor undergraduates in research activities (3 pages max), unofficial undergraduate and graduate transcripts, and complete contact information for three references. The statement of teaching philosophy should describe your inclusive teaching and mentoring efforts, broadly conceived, and how your teaching and mentoring may contribute to a liberal arts and sciences community that aims, among other things, to “honor inquiry, promote diversity, [and] strive for equity” ( FUture Focused ). You may also discuss any relevant professional development, service contributions, or other experiences that have refined your skills, or demonstrate your efforts in these areas.   Review of applications will begin on October 5, 2026, and continue until the positions are filled. Questions about this position may be directed to Adi Dubash, Associate Professor of Biology ( adi.dubash@furman.edu ).   Education Requirements: Certification Requirements: Job Posting End Date (if date is blank, posting is open ended):"
    },
    "https://furman.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/Furman_Careers/job/Main-Campus/Assistant--Associate--or-Professor-of-French-with-a-specialization-in-African-Francophone-Studies_R003356": {
      "title": "Assistant, Associate, or Professor of French with a specialization in African Francophone Studies",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-27\nFull time\n\nWelcome to Furman University's Career Site! IMPORTANT :​ Load all documents in the My Experience area under Resume/CV . This may include your resume/C.V., cover letter, unofficial transcript, teaching philosophy, etc. Please wait for all documents to finish uploading before clicking Next. If the process times out you will lose your progress, so please ensure you have all necessary documents available before starting. The drop-down lists only display so many options: please type into a drop-down list to search for your option. For example: in Field of Study, you may need to enter your field name. If you have no field, type \"None.\" If you have previously applied, make sure your information is current as you can transfer it to another application. Prior to submitting your application, verify all information for accuracy and ensure you have uploaded all appropriate documents.  Once submitted, you will not be able to edit your application other than to change your contact information. If you have any questions or need additional assistance, please contact the Office of Human Resources via email at recruitment@furman.edu  or by calling 864-294-3103. Job Title: Assistant, Associate, or Professor of French with a specialization in African Francophone Studies Job Family: Furman Faculty Full-Time/Part-Time: Full time Pay Type: Salary Department: Modern Languages & Literatures Job Summary: The Department of Modern Languages and Literatures at Furman University invites applications for a tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Professor of African Francophone Studies to begin August 1, 2027. The successful candidate will join a thriving French program marked by rapid growth in majors, rich opportunities for experiential learning, and a strong commitment to teaching excellence. We seek an innovative, dynamic teacher-scholar to develop a curricular focus on the Francophone African world. We are inviting candidates with expertise in Francophone Africa and/or the Francophone African Diaspora who will successfully engage students at all levels of French language courses as well as in a variety of advanced-level content courses within the French major. Area of specialization within African Francophone Studies is open and could include expertise in subfields such as ecocriticism, film, new media, digital humanities, cultural studies, gender and sexuality studies, race and ethnicity studies, or literature. Other subfields and topics are also welcomed. Job Description: The teaching load is five courses per year, which will include language classes at all levels. The successful candidate will become an integral part of both the French program and the department of Modern Languages and Literatures at Furman. They will be expected to develop courses in their area of expertise, be actively involved in co-curricular programming and French Language House supervision, play an active role in French program recruiting efforts, coordinate study abroad as needed, and teach first-year seminar courses. The successful candidate is also expected to maintain an active research agenda, advise, mentor, become an energetic contributor to The Furman Advantage ( https://www.furman.edu/furman-advantage/ ) and undergraduate research, and participate in department/university service. Qualified candidates must demonstrate a commitment to and excellence in undergraduate instruction at all levels as well as excellence in research, with a promising record of publications. Qualifications include a Ph.D. in French and Francophone Studies, or a related field, expected by August 1, 2027. A minimum of two years of experience teaching at the university level is preferred. Native or near-native level language proficiency in French and English is required. The position offers competitive salary and benefits. The successful candidate will have the ability to work with students from diverse backgrounds and contribute to Furman’s commitment to expanding access and opportunity to Furman’s rich learning culture. Furman University is dedicated to fostering a vibrant and inclusive community through excellence in teaching, mentorship, scholarship, and programming. We believe that cultural understanding, inclusiveness, and freedom of inquiry, thought, and discourse are essential components of a transformative undergraduate education. We advance these ideals with a liberal arts and sciences curriculum built on a substantial general education program, featuring traditional and innovative elements, and a robust portfolio of disciplinary and interdisciplinary major and minor areas of study. Additionally, we have established and continue to develop various initiatives, including historic projects, dialogue programs such as On Discourse and the Intergroup Dialogues Program, the Center for Interpersonal Connections, and four distinctive external facing institutes. Application instructions: Applicants should submit materials no later than November 1st, 2026. Preliminary interviews will be conducted remotely via video conference. Applications received after November 1st will be reviewed on a rolling basis until November 20th. While we encourage excellent applicants to submit their completed materials at any point, we cannot guarantee full consideration of late applications. Please upload all application materials as a single PDF in the following order : letter of interest, CV, statement of teaching philosophy, evidence of excellence in teaching (of no more than 10 pages), a writing sample of no more than 20 pages, and contact information for three references (at least one of which must be able to address the candidate’s teaching abilities). References will be contacted at later stages of the search for candidates who advance. The statement of teaching philosophy should describe your inclusive teaching and mentoring efforts, broadly conceived, and how your teaching and mentoring may contribute to a liberal arts and sciences community that aims, among other things, to “honor inquiry, promote diversity, [and] strive for equity” ( FUture Focused ). You may also discuss any relevant professional development, service contributions, or other experiences that have refined your skills or demonstrate your efforts in these areas. Inquiries may be directed to Dr. Ronald J. Friis, Chair, Department of Modern Languages and Literatures, Furman University, 3300 Poinsett Highway, Greenville, SC 29613. Education Requirements: Certification Requirements: Job Posting End Date (if date is blank, posting is open ended):"
    },
    "https://furman.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/Furman_Careers/job/Main-Campus/Professor-of-Japanese--Assistant-Associate-Full-_R003312": {
      "title": "Professor of Japanese (Assistant/Associate/Full)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-10\nFull time\n\nWelcome to Furman University's Career Site! IMPORTANT :​ Load all documents in the My Experience area under Resume/CV . This may include your resume/C.V., cover letter, unofficial transcript, teaching philosophy, etc. Please wait for all documents to finish uploading before clicking Next. If the process times out you will lose your progress, so please ensure you have all necessary documents available before starting. The drop-down lists only display so many options: please type into a drop-down list to search for your option. For example: in Field of Study, you may need to enter your field name. If you have no field, type \"None.\" If you have previously applied, make sure your information is current as you can transfer it to another application. Prior to submitting your application, verify all information for accuracy and ensure you have uploaded all appropriate documents.  Once submitted, you will not be able to edit your application other than to change your contact information. If you have any questions or need additional assistance, please contact the Office of Human Resources via email at recruitment@furman.edu  or by calling 864-294-3103. Job Title: Professor of Japanese (Assistant/Associate/Full) Job Family: Furman Faculty Full-Time/Part-Time: Full time Pay Type: Salary Department: Asian Studies Job Summary: The Department of Asian Studies at Furman University invites applications for a tenure-track position at the rank of assistant, associate, or professor of Japanese to begin August 2027. The position consists primarily in teaching Japanese language, and candidates must demonstrate significant experience, excellence, and enthusiasm in Japanese language instruction. We seek applicants with expertise in the fields of Japanese culture and society, including but not limited to film or performing arts, literature, gender and sexuality, or race and ethnicity. Candidates who also possess training in language pedagogical methods are especially encouraged to apply. Teaching load is five courses per year, which will include language classes at all levels. Responsibilities also include developing courses in the candidate’s area of specialty, coordinating study abroad; involvement in co-curricular activities; teaching first-year seminars; pursuing an active research agenda; advising and mentoring; and university service. Minimum qualifications include a Ph.D. in Japanese or a related field expected by Aug 1, 2027. Native language proficiency or near-native language proficiency in Japanese and English is required. Candidates must demonstrate both excellence in teaching and scholarly potential. Job Description: The Department of Asian Studies at Furman University invites applications for a tenure-track position at the rank of assistant, associate, or professor of Japanese to begin August 2027. The successful candidate will join one of the largest Asian Studies departments among liberal arts undergraduate institutions, with a vibrant, interdisciplinary program and a strong commitment to engaged learning. The position consists primarily in teaching Japanese language, and candidates must demonstrate significant experience, excellence, and enthusiasm in Japanese language instruction. We seek applicants with expertise in the fields of Japanese culture and society, including but not limited to film or performing arts, literature, gender and sexuality, or race and ethnicity. Candidates who also possess training in language pedagogical methods are especially encouraged to apply. The successful candidate will become an integral part of the Japanese language program at Furman. Teaching load is five courses per year, which will include language classes at all levels. Responsibilities also include developing courses in the candidate’s area of specialty, coordinating study abroad; involvement in co-curricular activities; teaching first-year seminars; pursuing an active research agenda; advising and mentoring; and university service. Minimum qualifications include a Ph.D. in Japanese or a related field expected by Aug 1, 2027. Native language proficiency or near-native language proficiency in Japanese and English is required. Candidates must demonstrate both excellence in teaching and scholarly potential. Successful candidates will also show the potential to be dedicated contributors to The Furman Advantage ( https://www.furman.edu/furman-advantage/ ) and to promoting a diverse and inclusive teaching environment. The position offers competitive salary and benefits. Furman University is dedicated to fostering a vibrant and inclusive community through excellence in teaching, mentorship, scholarship, and programming. We believe that cultural understanding, inclusiveness, and freedom of inquiry, thought, and discourse are essential components of a transformative undergraduate education. We advance these ideals with a liberal arts and sciences curriculum built on a substantial general education program, featuring traditional and innovative elements, and a robust portfolio of disciplinary and interdisciplinary major and minor areas of study. Additionally, we have established and continue to develop various initiatives, including historic projects, dialogue programs such as On Discourse and the Intergroup Dialogues Program, the Center for Interpersonal Connections, and four distinctive external-facing institutes. The successful candidate will have the ability to work with students from diverse backgrounds and contribute to Furman’s commitment to expanding access and opportunity to Furman’s rich learning culture. Application instructions: Applicants must submit materials no later than October 1, 2026 as part of the application process. Applicants should submit the following documents as a single PDF in the order listed: a letter of interest, C.V., statement of teaching philosophy, and complete contact information for three references. The statement of teaching philosophy should describe your inclusive teaching and mentoring efforts, broadly conceived, and how your teaching and mentoring may contribute to a liberal arts and sciences community that aims, among other things, to “honor inquiry, promote diversity, [and] strive for equity” (FUture Focused). You may also discuss any relevant professional development, service contributions, or other experiences that have refined your skills or demonstrate your efforts in these areas. Preliminary interviews will be conducted remotely via video conference. Inquiries may be directed to Alexander Francis-Ratte, Chair of the Japanese Search Committee, Department of Asian Studies, Furman University, 3300 Poinsett Highway, Greenville, SC 29613, alexander.francis-ratte@furman.edu Education Requirements: Certification Requirements: Job Posting End Date (if date is blank, posting is open ended):"
    },
    "https://furman.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/Furman_Careers/job/Off-Campus/Child-Development-Center-Substitute-Teacher_R003338": {
      "title": "Child Development Center Substitute Teacher",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-12\nPart time\n\nWelcome to Furman University's Career Site! IMPORTANT :​ Load all documents in the My Experience area under Resume/CV . This may include your resume/C.V., cover letter, unofficial transcript, teaching philosophy, etc. Please wait for all documents to finish uploading before clicking Next. If the process times out you will lose your progress, so please ensure you have all necessary documents available before starting. The drop-down lists only display so many options: please type into a drop-down list to search for your option. For example: in Field of Study, you may need to enter your field name. If you have no field, type \"None.\" If you have previously applied, make sure your information is current as you can transfer it to another application. Prior to submitting your application, verify all information for accuracy and ensure you have uploaded all appropriate documents.  Once submitted, you will not be able to edit your application other than to change your contact information. If you have any questions or need additional assistance, please contact the Office of Human Resources via email at recruitment@furman.edu  or by calling 864-294-3103. Job Title: Child Development Center Substitute Teacher Job Family: Temp Full-Time/Part-Time: Part time Pay Type: Hourly Department: JM Child Development Center Job Summary: To implement the educational program for preschool and/or kindergarten students at Furman’s Child Development Center, using knowledge of child development and best practices. Job Description: Furman University is now accepting applications for an energetic, experienced substitute for preschoolers and kindergartners.  Applicants must have prior experience working with young children in a childcare setting.  A substitute would be contacted as needed and would be responsible for following classroom lesson plans and all guidelines set forth by DSS licensing and the CDC director.  Please submit application, a resume and two letters of reference for consideration. Hours: Variable from 7:30am-5:30pm, as needed Monday-Friday Education Requirements: Certification Requirements: Job Posting End Date (if date is blank, posting is open ended):"
    },
    "https://furman.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/Furman_Careers/job/Main-Campus/Assistant-Associate-Full-Professor-of-Philosophy_R003339": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Philosophy",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-11\nFull time\n\nWelcome to Furman University's Career Site! IMPORTANT :​ Load all documents in the My Experience area under Resume/CV . This may include your resume/C.V., cover letter, unofficial transcript, teaching philosophy, etc. Please wait for all documents to finish uploading before clicking Next. If the process times out you will lose your progress, so please ensure you have all necessary documents available before starting. The drop-down lists only display so many options: please type into a drop-down list to search for your option. For example: in Field of Study, you may need to enter your field name. If you have no field, type \"None.\" If you have previously applied, make sure your information is current as you can transfer it to another application. Prior to submitting your application, verify all information for accuracy and ensure you have uploaded all appropriate documents.  Once submitted, you will not be able to edit your application other than to change your contact information. If you have any questions or need additional assistance, please contact the Office of Human Resources via email at recruitment@furman.edu  or by calling 864-294-3103. Job Title: Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Philosophy Job Family: Furman Faculty Full-Time/Part-Time: Full time Pay Type: Salary Department: Philosophy Job Summary: The Department of Philosophy at Furman University invites applications for the position of Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Philosophy, beginning August 1, 2027. Area of Specialization: History of Philosophy (Ancient Greek and Roman Philosophy, Medieval and Renaissance Philosophy, Arabic and Islamic Philosophy, or Early Modern Philosophy); Area of Competence: Open. The department has need for courses across a wide range of pre-19th century contexts, so candidates who can teach in more than one historical period would be particularly welcome. In addition to their areas of specialized research, the successful candidate will have broad philosophical interests and will be a dynamic and engaging teacher committed to working with students with diverse interests and backgrounds. Job Description: The successful candidate will teach five courses per academic year, including both introductory and upper-level offerings. All members of the department are expected to teach at least one section of “Introduction to Philosophy” annually, as well as periodic First-Year Writing (FYW) seminars on a topic of the candidate’s choosing. The department will be particularly interested in candidates whose teaching engages the history of philosophy in innovative ways, with the potential for intersections with one or more of Furman’s interdisciplinary minors. Furman University is a selective private liberal arts and sciences college. Furman professors are exceptional teacher-scholars who mentor undergraduate students within a campus community that values and encourages diverse ideas and perspectives. A Ph.D. in Philosophy is required by August 1, 2027. Applicants should submit the following documents as a single PDF in the order listed: a letter of interest, C.V., statement of teaching philosophy, and evidence of innovative teaching. In addition, please arrange for three letters of reference to be sent on your behalf, either by mail or email to david.fink@furman.edu . The statement of teaching philosophy should describe your inclusive teaching and mentoring efforts, broadly conceived, and how your teaching and mentoring may contribute to a liberal arts and sciences community that aims, among other things, to “honor inquiry, promote diversity, [and] strive for equity” (FUture Focused). You may also discuss any relevant professional development, service contributions, or other experiences that have refined your skills or demonstrate your efforts in these areas. In addition, please include teaching evaluations (if available), sample syllabi (if available), and at least one writing sample (preferably single-authored). Additional materials may be requested at later stages of the search process for candidates who advance. Furman University is dedicated to fostering a vibrant and inclusive community through excellence in teaching, mentorship, and programming. We believe that cultural understanding, inclusiveness, and freedom of inquiry, thought, and discourse are essential components of a transformative undergraduate education. We advance these ideals with a liberal arts and sciences curriculum built on a substantial general education program, featuring traditional and innovative elements, and a robust portfolio of disciplinary and interdisciplinary major and minor areas of study. Additionally, we have established and continue to develop various initiatives, including historic projects, dialogue programs such as On Discourse and the Intergroup Dialogues Program, the Center for Interpersonal Connections, and four distinctive external-facing institutes. The successful candidate will have the ability to work with students from diverse backgrounds and contribute to Furman’s commitment to expanding access and opportunity to Furman’s rich learning culture. Furman is located in Greenville, South Carolina, one of the fastest-growing cities in the Southeast and consistently ranked among “America’s Ten Best” by  Forbes . The city boasts a vibrant downtown with top-tier restaurants, parks, shops, museums, galleries, music venues, and theaters. It also features an extensive network of nonprofits, international corporations, and excellent public and private schools. The surrounding region offers abundant outdoor recreation, including lakes, rivers, and mountains. Greenville is just 2½ hours from Atlanta, 1½ hours from Charlotte, and one hour from Asheville, North Carolina. A 20-mile bike and pedestrian trail connects Furman’s campus to downtown Greenville and to the nearby town of Travelers Rest—named one of “America's Coolest Small Towns.” The newly renovated Greenville-Spartanburg International Airport, located just 25 minutes from campus, offers daily service to major cities. Review of applications will begin on October 16 and continue until the position is filled.   Questions may be directed to the Chair of the Philosophy Department, Professor David Fink:  david.fink@furman.edu Education Requirements: Certification Requirements: Job Posting End Date (if date is blank, posting is open ended):"
    },
    "https://furman.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/Furman_Careers/job/Main-Campus/Professor-of-Chinese--Assistant-Associate-Full-_R003322": {
      "title": "Professor of Chinese (Assistant/Associate/Full)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-11\nFull time\n\nWelcome to Furman University's Career Site! IMPORTANT :​ Load all documents in the My Experience area under Resume/CV . This may include your resume/C.V., cover letter, unofficial transcript, teaching philosophy, etc. Please wait for all documents to finish uploading before clicking Next. If the process times out you will lose your progress, so please ensure you have all necessary documents available before starting. The drop-down lists only display so many options: please type into a drop-down list to search for your option. For example: in Field of Study, you may need to enter your field name. If you have no field, type \"None.\" If you have previously applied, make sure your information is current as you can transfer it to another application. Prior to submitting your application, verify all information for accuracy and ensure you have uploaded all appropriate documents.  Once submitted, you will not be able to edit your application other than to change your contact information. If you have any questions or need additional assistance, please contact the Office of Human Resources via email at recruitment@furman.edu  or by calling 864-294-3103. Job Title: Professor of Chinese (Assistant/Associate/Full) Job Family: Furman Faculty Full-Time/Part-Time: Full time Pay Type: Salary Department: Asian Studies Job Summary: The Department of Asian Studies at Furman University invites applications for a tenure-track position at the rank of assistant, associate, or professor of Chinese to begin August 2027. Candidates must demonstrate a record of effective teaching and student engagement in Chinese language instruction. The successful candidate will also teach courses in their field of Chinese Studies (specialization open) to complement our departmental offerings, such as cultural studies, film, literature, or other related fields. The successful candidate will teach five courses per year, which will include language classes at various levels and content courses in the candidate’s area of expertise. Responsibilities also include collaborating with colleagues to strengthen and expand the Chinese program through curriculum development, student advising and mentoring, and shared program coordination. The position is also responsible for directing study abroad, teaching first-year seminars, offering interdisciplinary courses on Asian Studies, pursuing an active research agenda, and performing university service. The successful candidate will join one of the largest Asian Studies departments among liberal arts undergraduate institutions, with a strong commitment to engaged learning and interdisciplinary teaching. Qualifications include a Ph.D. in Chinese or a related field expected by Aug 1, 2027. Native or near-native fluency in Mandarin Chinese and English is required. Candidates must demonstrate excellence in teaching and promoting an engaged and inclusive teaching environment and show strong potential for scholarly achievement. Successful candidates will also demonstrate the potential to be dedicated contributors to The Furman Advantage (https://www.furman.edu/furman-advantage/). The position offers competitive salary and benefits. Job Description: The Department of Asian Studies at Furman University invites applications for a tenure-track position at the rank of assistant, associate, or professor of Chinese to begin August 2027. Candidates must demonstrate a record of effective teaching and student engagement in Chinese language instruction. The successful candidate will also teach courses in their field of Chinese Studies (specialization open) to complement our departmental offerings, such as cultural studies, film, literature, or other related fields. The successful candidate will teach five courses per year, which will include language classes at various levels and content courses in the candidate’s area of expertise. Responsibilities also include collaborating with colleagues to strengthen and expand the Chinese program through curriculum development, student advising and mentoring, and shared program coordination. The position is also responsible for directing study abroad, teaching first-year seminars, offering interdisciplinary courses on Asian Studies, pursuing an active research agenda, and performing university service. The successful candidate will join one of the largest Asian Studies departments among liberal arts undergraduate institutions, with a strong commitment to engaged learning and interdisciplinary teaching. Qualifications include a Ph.D. in Chinese or a related field expected by Aug 1, 2027. Native or near-native fluency in Mandarin Chinese and English is required. Candidates must demonstrate excellence in teaching and promoting an engaged and inclusive teaching environment and show strong potential for scholarly achievement. Successful candidates will also demonstrate the potential to be dedicated contributors to The Furman Advantage ( https://www.furman.edu/furman-advantage/ ). The position offers competitive salary and benefits. Furman University is dedicated to fostering a vibrant and inclusive community through excellence in teaching, mentorship, scholarship, and programming. We believe that cultural understanding, inclusiveness, and freedom of inquiry, thought, and discourse are essential components of a transformative undergraduate education. We advance these ideals with a liberal arts and sciences curriculum built on a substantial general education program, featuring traditional and innovative elements, and a robust portfolio of disciplinary and interdisciplinary major and minor areas of study. Additionally, we have established and continue to develop various initiatives, including historic projects, dialogue programs such as On Discourse and the Intergroup Dialogues Program, the Center for Interpersonal Connections, and four distinctive external-facing institutes. The successful candidate will have the ability to work with students from diverse backgrounds and contribute to Furman’s commitment to expanding access and opportunity to Furman’s rich learning culture. Application instructions: Applicants must submit materials no later than October 1, 2026 through this link on the Furman University application portal: [     ]. Applicants should submit the following documents as a single PDF in the order listed: a letter of interest, C.V., statement of teaching philosophy, and complete contact information for three references. The statement of teaching philosophy should describe your inclusive teaching and mentoring efforts, broadly conceived, and how your teaching and mentoring may contribute to a liberal arts and sciences community that aims, among other things, to “honor inquiry, promote diversity, [and] strive for equity” (FUture Focused). You may also discuss any relevant professional development, service contributions, or other experiences that have refined your skills or demonstrate your efforts in these areas. Preliminary interviews will be conducted remotely via video conference. Inquiries may be directed to Dongming Zhang, Chair of the Chinese Search Committee, Department of Asian Studies, Furman University, 3300 Poinsett Highway, Greenville, SC 29613, dongming.zhang@furman.edu . Education Requirements: Certification Requirements: Job Posting End Date (if date is blank, posting is open ended):"
    },
    "https://furman.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/Furman_Careers/job/Main-Campus/Tocqueville-Center-Assistant-Director-and-Assistant-Professor-of-Classical-Liberal-Thought_R003269": {
      "title": "Tocqueville Center Assistant Director and Assistant Professor of Classical Liberal Thought",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-11\nFull time\n\nWelcome to Furman University's Career Site! IMPORTANT :​ Load all documents in the My Experience area under Resume/CV . This may include your resume/C.V., cover letter, unofficial transcript, teaching philosophy, etc. Please wait for all documents to finish uploading before clicking Next. If the process times out you will lose your progress, so please ensure you have all necessary documents available before starting. The drop-down lists only display so many options: please type into a drop-down list to search for your option. For example: in Field of Study, you may need to enter your field name. If you have no field, type \"None.\" If you have previously applied, make sure your information is current as you can transfer it to another application. Prior to submitting your application, verify all information for accuracy and ensure you have uploaded all appropriate documents.  Once submitted, you will not be able to edit your application other than to change your contact information. If you have any questions or need additional assistance, please contact the Office of Human Resources via email at recruitment@furman.edu  or by calling 864-294-3103. Job Title: Tocqueville Center Assistant Director and Assistant Professor of Classical Liberal Thought Job Family: Furman Faculty Full-Time/Part-Time: Full time Pay Type: Salary Department: Tocqueville Center Job Summary: The Tocqueville Center at Furman University invites applications for the position of Assistant/Associate Director, with a tenure-track appointment at the rank of Assistant/Associate/Full Professor in Classical Liberal Thought, beginning August 1, 2027. We seek candidates with expertise in the history of liberal thought, particularly focusing on eighteenth- and nineteenth-century British, French, and American Enlightenment thinkers. Job Description: The successful candidate will teach four courses per academic year, including both introductory and upper-level offerings, and will carry out administrative responsibilities at the Tocqueville Center. These duties include student programming and mentorship, event coordination, and media outreach. Furman University is a selective private liberal arts and sciences college. Furman professors are exceptional teacher-scholars who mentor undergraduate students within a campus community that values and encourages diverse ideas and perspectives. A Ph.D. in Political Thought or a related field is required by August 1, 2027. Applicants should submit the following documents as a single PDF in the order listed: a letter of interest, C.V., statement of teaching philosophy, and complete contact information for three references. The statement of teaching philosophy should describe your inclusive teaching and mentoring efforts, broadly conceived, and how your teaching and mentoring may contribute to a liberal arts and sciences community that aims, among other things, to “honor inquiry, promote diversity, [and] strive for equity” (FUture Focused). You may also discuss any relevant professional development, service contributions, or other experiences that have refined your skills or demonstrate your efforts in these areas. In addition, please include teaching evaluations (if available), sample syllabi (if available), and at least one writing sample (preferably single-authored). Additional materials may be requested at later stages of the search process for candidates who advance. The  Tocqueville Center for the Study of Democracy and Society  promotes the core principles of a free society—individual liberty, limited government, and freedom of speech—through rigorous academic inquiry. Established in 2008 as a program within the Department of Politics and International Affairs, the Center has since grown into an independent academic unit, gaining greater autonomy, interdisciplinary scope, and programmatic flexibility. This transition has allowed the Center to expand its influence across campus and disciplines. It plays a central role in fostering viewpoint diversity and scholarly engagement, most visibly through its prominent speaker series. The Tocqueville Fellows Program, a fully endowed, interdisciplinary initiative, supports 25 undergraduate students who engage year-round with visiting scholars and classic texts in intimate seminar settings. The Center’s recent elevation reflects the strong backing of Furman’s president and Board of Trustees and affirms the university’s commitment to increasing its national impact. For more information, consult the Center’s website at: https://www.furman.edu/academics/tocqueville-program/ Furman University is dedicated to fostering a vibrant and inclusive community through excellence in teaching, mentorship, and programming. We believe that cultural understanding, inclusiveness, and freedom of inquiry, thought, and discourse are essential components of a transformative undergraduate education. We advance these ideals with a liberal arts and sciences curriculum built on a substantial general education program, featuring traditional and innovative elements, and a robust portfolio of disciplinary and interdisciplinary major and minor areas of study. Additionally, we have established and continue to develop various initiatives, including historic projects, dialogue programs such as On Discourse and the Intergroup Dialogues Program, the Center for Interpersonal Connections, and four distinctive external-facing institutes. The successful candidate will have the ability to work with students from diverse backgrounds and contribute to Furman’s commitment to expanding access and opportunity to Furman’s rich learning culture. Furman is located in Greenville, South Carolina, one of the fastest-growing cities in the Southeast and consistently ranked among “America's Ten Best” by  Forbes . The city boasts a vibrant downtown with top-tier restaurants, parks, shops, museums, galleries, music venues, and theaters. It also features an extensive network of nonprofits, international corporations, and excellent public and private schools. The surrounding region offers abundant outdoor recreation, including lakes, rivers, and mountains. Greenville is just 2½ hours from Atlanta, 1½ hours from Charlotte, and one hour from Asheville, North Carolina. A 20-mile bike and pedestrian trail connects Furman’s campus to downtown Greenville and to the nearby town of Travelers Rest—named one of “America's Coolest Small Towns.” The newly renovated Greenville-Spartanburg International Airport, located just 25 minutes from campus, offers daily service to major cities. Review of applications will begin on October 2nd and continue until the position is filled. Questions may be directed to the search committee co-chairs: Professor Brent Nelsen: brent.nelsen@furman.edu Professor David Fink: david.fink@furman.edu Education Requirements: Doctorate: Political Science (Required) Certification Requirements: Job Posting End Date (if date is blank, posting is open ended):"
    },
    "https://furman.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/Furman_Careers/job/Main-Campus/Assistant--Associate-or-Full-Professor-of-Chemistry_R003326": {
      "title": "Assistant, Associate or Full Professor of Chemistry",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-07\nFull time\n\nWelcome to Furman University's Career Site! IMPORTANT :​ Load all documents in the My Experience area under Resume/CV . This may include your resume/C.V., cover letter, unofficial transcript, teaching philosophy, etc. Please wait for all documents to finish uploading before clicking Next. If the process times out you will lose your progress, so please ensure you have all necessary documents available before starting. The drop-down lists only display so many options: please type into a drop-down list to search for your option. For example: in Field of Study, you may need to enter your field name. If you have no field, type \"None.\" If you have previously applied, make sure your information is current as you can transfer it to another application. Prior to submitting your application, verify all information for accuracy and ensure you have uploaded all appropriate documents.  Once submitted, you will not be able to edit your application other than to change your contact information. If you have any questions or need additional assistance, please contact the Office of Human Resources via email at recruitment@furman.edu  or by calling 864-294-3103. Job Title: Assistant, Associate or Full Professor of Chemistry Job Family: Furman Faculty Full-Time/Part-Time: Full time Pay Type: Salary Department: Chemistry Job Summary: The Department of Chemistry at Furman University invites applications to fill a tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor in the area of inorganic chemistry to begin in August 2027. Applicants must hold a Ph.D. in inorganic chemistry or a closely related field with postdoctoral experience strongly preferred. Successful candidates are expected to excel in teaching at the undergraduate level, mentor and advise students, and conduct original research leading to peer-reviewed publications or other significant scholarly contributions to the discipline. The ideal candidate will also demonstrate the ability to work with students from diverse backgrounds and contribute to Furman’s commitment to expanding access and opportunity within our rich learning culture. Primary teaching responsibilities will be inorganic and general chemistry courses, with additional opportunities to teach advanced topics in the area of research specialization, lab-centered major’s courses, and chemistry for non-majors. The standard teaching load is 4-5 courses per academic year. Tenure-track faculty normally devote their summers to research with students and do not teach. Job Description: The Department of Chemistry at Furman University invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor.  A Ph.D. in inorganic chemistry or a related discipline is required by August 1, 2027; prior university-level teaching experience and post-doctoral experience are highly preferred but not required.  The successful candidate will join a vibrant and supportive department of 13 research active faculty.  Candidates must demonstrate commitment to teaching, service, and scholarship. Furman has a strong history of excellent teaching and mentoring, including a vigorous year-round research program with undergraduate students. Therefore, a faculty member is expected to establish a nationally competitive undergraduate research program. In support of this program, the department maintains state-of-the-art facilities with exceptional instrument holdings, including those in support of inorganic synthetic, photophysics, and materials research, among others.  Furman offers competitive start-up funds, individual research space, and summer support.   Furman University is dedicated to fostering a vibrant and inclusive community through excellence in teaching, mentorship, and programming. We believe that cultural understanding, inclusiveness, and freedom of inquiry, thought, and discourse are essential components of a transformative undergraduate education.We advance these ideals with a liberal arts and sciences curriculum built on a substantial general education program, featuring traditional and innovative elements, and a robust portfolio of disciplinary and interdisciplinary major and minor areas of study. Additionally, we have established and continue to develop various initiatives, including historic projects, dialogue programs such as On Discourse and the Intergroup Dialogues Program, the Center for Interpersonal Connections, and four distinctive external-facing institutes. The successful candidate will have the ability to work with students from diverse backgrounds and contribute to Furman’s commitment to expanding access and opportunity to Furman’s rich learning culture. Applicants should submit the following documents as a single PDF in the order listed: a letter of interest addressing your qualifications and commitment to a research active, undergraduate program. Include a description of how your teaching, scholarship, mentoring and/or service would contribute to a liberal arts college community (2 pages max); a complete curriculum vitae, undergraduate and graduate transcripts; a statement of teaching and research mentoring philosophy (2 pages max), a detailed research plan (4 pages max), and complete contact information for three references. The statement of teaching philosophy and interests should describe your inclusive teaching and mentoring efforts, broadly conceived, and how your teaching and mentoring may contribute to a liberal arts and sciences community that aims, among other things, to “honor inquiry, promote diversity, and strive for equity” ( FUture Focused ) .  Position commences August 1, 2027. Review of applications will begin immediately with priority consideration given to applications received by September 15, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled.  Education Requirements: Doctorate: Chemistry (Required) Education Requirements: Doctorate: Chemistry (Required) Certification Requirements: Job Posting End Date (if date is blank, posting is open ended):"
    },
    "https://furman.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/Furman_Careers/job/Main-Campus/Professor-Sociology_R003292": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Sociology",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-28\nFull time\n\nWelcome to Furman University's Career Site! IMPORTANT :​ Load all documents in the My Experience area under Resume/CV . This may include your resume/C.V., cover letter, unofficial transcript, teaching philosophy, etc. Please wait for all documents to finish uploading before clicking Next. If the process times out you will lose your progress, so please ensure you have all necessary documents available before starting. The drop-down lists only display so many options: please type into a drop-down list to search for your option. For example: in Field of Study, you may need to enter your field name. If you have no field, type \"None.\" If you have previously applied, make sure your information is current as you can transfer it to another application. Prior to submitting your application, verify all information for accuracy and ensure you have uploaded all appropriate documents.  Once submitted, you will not be able to edit your application other than to change your contact information. If you have any questions or need additional assistance, please contact the Office of Human Resources via email at recruitment@furman.edu  or by calling 864-294-3103. Job Title: Assistant Professor of Sociology Job Family: Furman Faculty Full-Time/Part-Time: Full time Pay Type: Salary Department: Sociology Job Summary: The Department of Sociology at Furman University invites applications for two Assistant/Associate/Professor tenure-track positions beginning August 1, 2027. We welcome candidates from any substantive area of sociology whose expertise complements and expands our existing departmental strengths, and whose work reflects a commitment to rigorous inquiry and meaningful engagement with students. A Ph.D. in Sociology is required by August 1, 2027. Job Description: We encourage applications from candidates who demonstrate a commitment to excellence in teaching, student mentorship, and research in a liberal arts environment. The teaching responsibility is five courses per academic year.  A strong application will articulate how the candidate envisions contributing to our core curriculum, which includes Introduction to Sociology, Sociological Theory, Qualitative and Quantitative Methods, and 200-level courses in the Sociology of Gender and Sexuality, Race/Ethnicity, or Social Class. Beyond core requirements, we welcome applicants who would bring new course offerings that deepen and diversify our curricular landscape and contribute to the goals of Furman University’s Strategic Plan. Applicants should submit the following documents in a single PDF in the order listed: a letter of interest, C.V., statement of teaching philosophy, and complete contact information for three references. The statement of teaching philosophy should describe your inclusive teaching and mentoring efforts, broadly conceived, and how your teaching and mentoring may contribute to a liberal arts and sciences community that aims, among other things, to “honor inquiry, promote diversity, [and] strive for equity” ( FUture Focused ) . You may also discuss any relevant professional development, service contributions, or other experiences that have refined your skills or demonstrate your efforts in these areas. Additional materials may be requested at later stages of the search process for candidates who advance. Furman University is dedicated to fostering a vibrant and inclusive community through excellence in teaching, mentorship, and programming. We believe that cultural understanding, inclusiveness, and freedom of inquiry, thought, and discourse are essential components of a transformative undergraduate education. We advance these ideals with a liberal arts and sciences curriculum built on a substantial general education program, featuring traditional and innovative elements, and a robust portfolio of disciplinary and interdisciplinary major and minor areas of study. Additionally, we have established and continue to develop various initiatives, including historic projects, dialogue programs such as On Discourse and the Intergroup Dialogues Program, the Center for Interpersonal Connections, and four distinctive external-facing institutes. The successful candidate will have the ability to work with students from diverse backgrounds and contribute to Furman’s commitment to expanding access and opportunity to Furman’s rich learning culture. Review of applications will begin on September 10, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Please direct inquiries to Kristy Maher, Acting Chair of Sociology, at kristy.maher@furman.edu Education Requirements: Certification Requirements: Job Posting End Date (if date is blank, posting is open ended):"
    },
    "https://furman.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/Furman_Careers/job/Main-Campus/Assistant-Professor-Classics_R003313": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Full  Professor of Classics",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-28\nFull time\n\nWelcome to Furman University's Career Site! IMPORTANT :​ Load all documents in the My Experience area under Resume/CV . This may include your resume/C.V., cover letter, unofficial transcript, teaching philosophy, etc. Please wait for all documents to finish uploading before clicking Next. If the process times out you will lose your progress, so please ensure you have all necessary documents available before starting. The drop-down lists only display so many options: please type into a drop-down list to search for your option. For example: in Field of Study, you may need to enter your field name. If you have no field, type \"None.\" If you have previously applied, make sure your information is current as you can transfer it to another application. Prior to submitting your application, verify all information for accuracy and ensure you have uploaded all appropriate documents.  Once submitted, you will not be able to edit your application other than to change your contact information. If you have any questions or need additional assistance, please contact the Office of Human Resources via email at recruitment@furman.edu  or by calling 864-294-3103. Job Title: Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Classics Job Family: Furman Faculty Full-Time/Part-Time: Full time Pay Type: Salary Department: Classics Job Summary: The Department of Classics at Furman University invites applications for a tenure-track position of Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Classics, beginning August 1, 2027. We seek a broadly-trained classicist with expertise in any of the following areas: Latin prose, Roman history, social history, historiography, Tacitus, Cicero. Job Description: The Department of Classics welcomes applications from candidates who value as we do an integrated approach to teaching, collaborative learning, and scholarship. We seek a broadly-trained classicist with expertise in any of the following areas: Latin prose, Roman history, social history, historiography, Tacitus, Cicero. Candidates must have a thoughtful approach to teaching Greek and Latin, to the rigorous application of technology to humanism, and to engaging the broadest possible community in the study of the ancient world.  Applicants should be prepared to teach a wide range of undergraduate courses in our curriculum, including Greek and Latin at all levels of instruction and thematic courses in classical civilization and culture. The teaching load is five courses over two semesters. Other duties include mentoring and collaborating with undergraduate students on research projects, and contributing to the administrative responsibilities of the Department and the University. A Ph.D. in Classics or a related field is required by August 1, 2027. The deadline for application is October 31, 2026. Review of applications will begin immediately. We will conduct initial interviews by Zoom in late November or early December.  Questions may be directed to the search committee chair, Randall Childree ( randall.childree@furman.edu ).  Required Documents Applicants should submit the following documents as a single PDF in the order listed: 1. Letter of interest 2. C.V. 3. Statement of teaching philosophy, and 4. Complete contact information for three references. In the letter of interest, describe how you would teach an upper-level Latin language course and a topical Roman-themed course aimed at the general-education student, and how you would foster undergraduate research. The statement of teaching philosophy should describe your inclusive teaching and mentoring efforts, broadly conceived, and how your teaching and mentoring may contribute to a liberal arts and sciences community that aims, among other things, to “honor inquiry, promote diversity, [and] strive for equity” (FUture Focused). You may also discuss any relevant professional development, service contributions, or other experiences that have refined your skills or that demonstrate your efforts in these areas. About Furman University Furman University is dedicated to fostering a vibrant and inclusive community through excellence in teaching, mentorship, scholarship, and programming. We believe that cultural understanding, inclusiveness, and freedom of inquiry, thought, and discourse are essential components of a transformative undergraduate education.  We advance these ideals with a liberal arts and sciences curriculum built on a substantial general education program, featuring traditional and innovative elements, and a robust portfolio of disciplinary and interdisciplinary major and minor areas of study. Additionally, we have established and continue to develop various initiatives, including historic projects, dialogue programs such as On Discourse and the Intergroup Dialogues Program, the Center for Interpersonal Connections, and four distinctive external-facing institutes. The successful candidate will have the ability to work with students from diverse backgrounds and contribute to Furman’s commitment to expanding access and opportunity to Furman’s rich learning culture. Education Requirements: Certification Requirements: Job Posting End Date (if date is blank, posting is open ended):"
    },
    "https://furman.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/Furman_Careers/job/Main-Campus/Assistant--Associate--or-Full-Professor-of-Analytics_R003303": {
      "title": "Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor of Analytics",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-27\nFull time\n\nWelcome to Furman University's Career Site! IMPORTANT :​ Load all documents in the My Experience area under Resume/CV . This may include your resume/C.V., cover letter, unofficial transcript, teaching philosophy, etc. Please wait for all documents to finish uploading before clicking Next. If the process times out you will lose your progress, so please ensure you have all necessary documents available before starting. The drop-down lists only display so many options: please type into a drop-down list to search for your option. For example: in Field of Study, you may need to enter your field name. If you have no field, type \"None.\" If you have previously applied, make sure your information is current as you can transfer it to another application. Prior to submitting your application, verify all information for accuracy and ensure you have uploaded all appropriate documents.  Once submitted, you will not be able to edit your application other than to change your contact information. If you have any questions or need additional assistance, please contact the Office of Human Resources via email at recruitment@furman.edu  or by calling 864-294-3103. Job Title: Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor of Analytics Job Family: Furman Faculty Full-Time/Part-Time: Full time Pay Type: Salary Department: Business/Accounting Job Summary: The Business and Accounting Department at Furman University invites applications for a tenure-track position in Analytics at the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. This position is one of three newly approved faculty hires in business and accounting and will commence on August 1, 2027. Candidates with a strong interest in data analytics education within a nationally ranked liberal arts and science setting are encouraged to apply. Successful candidates are expected to excel in teaching at the undergraduate level, mentor and advise students, and conduct original research leading to peer-reviewed publications or other significant scholarly contributions to the discipline. The ideal candidate will also demonstrate the ability to work with students from diverse backgrounds and contribute to Furman’s commitment to expanding access and opportunity within our rich learning culture. The teaching load is five courses per year. In addition to the introductory and intermediate business analytics courses, the successful candidate will have the opportunity to teach advanced data analytics electives related to their area of expertise. Job Description: A Ph.D. or D.B.A. in data analytics, operations, business, or a related discipline is required by August 1, 2027; ABD candidates will be considered, provided the degree is conferred before that date. Prior university-level teaching experience and corporate or industry experience are highly preferred but not required.  The teaching load is five sections per academic year.  In addition to the introductory business analytics course, the candidate will have the opportunity to teach advanced business analytics electives related to their area of expertise. Successful candidates are expected to excel in teaching at the undergraduate level, mentor and advise students, and conduct original research leading to peer-reviewed publications or other significant scholarly contributions to the discipline. Duties also include service to the department and university. The Business and Accounting Department offers bachelor’s degrees in Accounting, Business, and Finance . Within the Business major, students can select a track in Entrepreneurship, Marketing, International Business, or Business Administration. The Business and Accounting Department also participates in and supports the Data and Decision Analytics major, and the interdisciplinary minors in Data Analytics and Visual Strategy. The ideal candidate will also demonstrate the ability to work with students from diverse backgrounds and contribute to Furman’s commitment to expanding access and opportunity within our rich learning culture. The ideal candidate will also be eager to develop high-impact, engaged learning experiences, including directing and mentoring undergraduate research and course-related projects. The department has a history of community engaged learning. There are currently 10 full-time business and accounting faculty members.  The Joe & Diana Hurley Finance & Business Analytics Lab provides students and faculty with access to Bloomberg terminals and Capital IQ. Faculty receive robust research support, including access to statistical analysis tools such as SAS, STATA, SPSS, and ArcGIS, alongside institutional subscriptions to The Wall Street Journal and Bloomberg news. Furman University is dedicated to fostering a vibrant and inclusive community through excellence in teaching, mentorship, and programming. We believe that cultural understanding, inclusiveness, and freedom of inquiry, thought, and discourse are essential components of a transformative undergraduate education. We advance these ideals with a liberal arts and sciences curriculum built on a substantial general education program, featuring traditional and innovative elements, and a robust portfolio of disciplinary and interdisciplinary major and minor areas of study. Additionally, we have established and continue to develop various initiatives, including historic projects, dialogue programs such as On Discourse and the Intergroup Dialogues Program, the Center for Interpersonal Connections, and four distinctive external facing institutes. Applicants should submit the following documents as a single PDF in the order listed: a letter of interest, curriculum vitae , statement of teaching philosophy and interests, statement of research, and complete contact information for three references. The statement of teaching philosophy and interests should describe your inclusive teaching and mentoring efforts, broadly conceived, and how your teaching and mentoring may contribute to a liberal arts and sciences community that aims, among other things, to “honor inquiry, promote diversity, [and] strive for equity” ( FUture Focused ) . You may also discuss any relevant professional development, service contributions, or other experiences that have refined your skills or demonstrate your efforts in these areas. While detailing your specific teaching interests discussion of your prior course experience and any industry background that can be leveraged to enhance classroom instruction and student mentorship is welcomed . The position commences on August 1, 2027. Review of applications will begin immediately, with priority consideration given to applications received by September 15, 2026, and the search will continue until the position is filled.   Please d irect any questions via email to the S earch C ommittee C hair , Dr. Virginia Gerde , a t virginia.gerde@furman.edu. Education Requirements: Certification Requirements: Job Posting End Date (if date is blank, posting is open ended):"
    },
    "https://furman.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/Furman_Careers/job/Main-Campus/Assistant--Associate-or-Full-Professor-of-Accounting_R003302": {
      "title": "Assistant, Associate or Full Professor of Accounting",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-27\nFull time\n\nWelcome to Furman University's Career Site! IMPORTANT :​ Load all documents in the My Experience area under Resume/CV . This may include your resume/C.V., cover letter, unofficial transcript, teaching philosophy, etc. Please wait for all documents to finish uploading before clicking Next. If the process times out you will lose your progress, so please ensure you have all necessary documents available before starting. The drop-down lists only display so many options: please type into a drop-down list to search for your option. For example: in Field of Study, you may need to enter your field name. If you have no field, type \"None.\" If you have previously applied, make sure your information is current as you can transfer it to another application. Prior to submitting your application, verify all information for accuracy and ensure you have uploaded all appropriate documents.  Once submitted, you will not be able to edit your application other than to change your contact information. If you have any questions or need additional assistance, please contact the Office of Human Resources via email at recruitment@furman.edu  or by calling 864-294-3103. Job Title: Assistant, Associate or Full Professor of Accounting Job Family: Furman Faculty Full-Time/Part-Time: Full time Pay Type: Salary Department: Business/Accounting Job Summary: The Business and Accounting Department at Furman University invites applications for a tenure-track position in Accounting at the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. This position is one of three newly approved faculty hires in business and accounting and will commence on August 1, 2027. Candidates with a strong interest in accounting education within a nationally ranked liberal arts and science setting are encouraged to apply. Successful candidates are expected to excel in teaching at the undergraduate level, mentor and advise students, and conduct original research leading to peer-reviewed publications or publication in outlets valued by active members of the profession or contribute to their discipline in other significant ways. The ideal candidate will also demonstrate the ability to work with students from diverse backgrounds and contribute to Furman’s commitment to expanding access and opportunity to Furman’s rich learning culture. The teaching load is five courses per year. The successful candidate will be able to teach both the introductory level course in managerial/financial accounting and advanced courses, including either federal income taxation or managerial accounting. Job Description: A Ph.D. or D.B.A. in accounting or a related discipline is required by August 1, 2027; ABD candidates will be considered, provided the degree is conferred before that date. Prior university-level teaching experience, professional accounting experience, and involvement in relevant professional organizations are preferred but not required.   The teaching load is five sections per academic year.  In addition to the introductory financial/managerial course, the successful candidate will be prepared to teach advanced courses including federal income taxation or managerial accounting. Successful candidates are expected to excel at teaching at the undergraduate level, mentor and advise students, and conduct original research leading to peer-reviewed publications or publication in outlets valued by active members of the profession or contribute to their discipline in other significant ways. Duties also include service to the department and university. The ideal candidate will also demonstrate the ability to work with students from diverse backgrounds and contribute to Furman’s commitment to expanding access and opportunity to Furman’s rich learning culture. The successful candidate will also be eager to develop high-impact engaged learning experiences for undergraduates, including directing research, mentoring, and directing students in course-related projects in the community.  The Business and Accounting Department offers bachelor’s degrees in Accounting, Business, and Finance .   Within the Business major, students select a track in Entrepreneurship, Marketing, International Business or Business Administration. The department also participates in interdisciplinary minors in Data Analytics and Visual Strategy, as well as community engaged courses.  There are currently 10 full-time business and accounting faculty members.  The Joe & Diana Hurley Finance & Business Analytics Lab provides students and faculty with access to Bloomberg terminals, and Capital IQ. Faculty receive research support and have access to statistical analysis tools such as SAS, STATA, SPSS, and ArcGIS, alongside institutional subscriptions to The Wall Street Journal and Bloomberg news. Furman University is dedicated to fostering a vibrant and inclusive community through excellence in teaching, mentorship, and programming. We believe that cultural understanding, inclusiveness, and freedom of inquiry, thought, and discourse are essential components of a transformative undergraduate education. We advance these ideals with a liberal arts and sciences curriculum built on a substantial general education program, featuring traditional and innovative elements, and a robust portfolio of disciplinary and interdisciplinary major and minor areas of study. Additionally, we have established and continue to develop various initiatives, including historic projects, dialogue programs such as On Discourse and the Intergroup Dialogues Program, the Center for Interpersonal Connections, and four distinctive external facing institutes. Applicants should submit the following documents as a single PDF in the order listed: a letter of interest, curriculum vitae , statement of teaching philosophy and interests, statement of research, and complete contact information for three references. The statement of teaching philosophy and interests should describe your inclusive teaching and mentoring efforts, broadly conceived, and how your teaching and mentoring may contribute to a liberal arts and sciences community that aims, among other things, to “honor inquiry, promote diversity, [and] strive for equity” ( FUture Focused ) . You may also discuss any relevant professional development, service contributions, or other experiences that have refined your skills or demonstrate your efforts in these areas. While detailing your specific teaching interests, discussion of your prior course experience and any industry background that can be leveraged to enhance classroom instruction and student mentorship is welcomed . Position commences August 1, 2027. Review of applications will begin immediately with priority consideration given to applications received by September 15, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled.  Direct your questions by email to search committee chair Professor Sandy Roberson, CPA, at sandy.roberson@furman.edu . Education Requirements: Certification Requirements: Job Posting End Date (if date is blank, posting is open ended):"
    },
    "https://furman.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/Furman_Careers/job/Main-Campus/Tenure-Track-Position-in-Social-or-Social-CognitivePsychology_R003308": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track Position in Social or Social Cognitive Psychology",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-23\nFull time\n\nWelcome to Furman University's Career Site! IMPORTANT :​ Load all documents in the My Experience area under Resume/CV . This may include your resume/C.V., cover letter, unofficial transcript, teaching philosophy, etc. Please wait for all documents to finish uploading before clicking Next. If the process times out you will lose your progress, so please ensure you have all necessary documents available before starting. The drop-down lists only display so many options: please type into a drop-down list to search for your option. For example: in Field of Study, you may need to enter your field name. If you have no field, type \"None.\" If you have previously applied, make sure your information is current as you can transfer it to another application. Prior to submitting your application, verify all information for accuracy and ensure you have uploaded all appropriate documents.  Once submitted, you will not be able to edit your application other than to change your contact information. If you have any questions or need additional assistance, please contact the Office of Human Resources via email at recruitment@furman.edu  or by calling 864-294-3103. Job Title: Tenure-Track Position in Social or Social Cognitive Psychology Job Family: Furman Faculty Full-Time/Part-Time: Full time Pay Type: Salary Department: Psychology Job Summary: The Psychology Department at Furman University invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor. Candidates must have expertise in social or social cognitive psychology and be committed to excellent teaching and producing high-quality research with undergraduate collaborators. A Ph.D. in Psychology is required by the position’s start date of August 1, 2027. Job Description: The Psychology Department at Furman University invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor. Candidates must have expertise in social or social cognitive psychology and be committed to excellent teaching and producing high-quality research with undergraduate collaborators. A Ph.D. in Psychology is required by the position’s start date of August 1, 2027. The successful candidate will join a vibrant and supportive department with outstanding teaching and research resources. Candidates will teach courses in stereotyping, prejudice, and discrimination, along with introductory psychology and research methods and statistics. They may also have the opportunity to teach other courses that support or expand the department’s curriculum, including a first-year writing seminar. The teaching load is five courses per year, split over two semesters. Faculty are also expected to serve as research mentors to undergraduate students throughout the academic year and during the summer. We offer competitive start-up funds, research space, and summer support. Founded in 1826, Furman University is a highly ranked liberal arts college that offers all students an integrated four-year pathway preparing them for lives of purpose and impact. The psychology major is known for its rigorous coursework, exceptional mentoring and advising, and numerous opportunities for high-impact, engaged learning experiences (e.g. research, internships, and travel study) supported by university resources. More information about the department is available at furman.edu/academics/psychology. Furman University is dedicated to fostering a vibrant and inclusive community through excellence in teaching, mentorship, and programming. We believe that cultural understanding, inclusiveness, and freedom of inquiry, thought, and discourse are essential components of a transformative undergraduate education. We advance these ideals with a liberal arts and sciences curriculum built on a substantial general education program, featuring traditional and innovative elements, and a robust portfolio of disciplinary and interdisciplinary major and minor areas of study. Additionally, we have established and continue to develop various initiatives, including historic projects, dialogue programs such as On Discourse and the Intergroup Dialogues Program, the Center for Interpersonal Connections, and four distinctive external-facing institutes. The successful candidate will have the ability to work with students from diverse backgrounds and contribute to Furman’s commitment to expanding access and opportunity to Furman’s rich learning culture. Furman is located in Greenville, South Carolina, one of the fastest-growing cities in the Southeast and is ranked among \"America's Ten Best\" by Forbes Magazine. The thriving downtown features excellent restaurants, in-town parks, shops, museums, galleries, music venues, and theaters. Greenville also enjoys an impressive network of nonprofits, small businesses, and international corporations. The city also has excellent public and private schools and a vibrant international community. A 20-mile bike and running trail connects the university to Greenville and to Travelers Rest, which was named \"one of America's coolest small towns.\" The surrounding area abounds with outdoor recreational activities and has some of the country's most beautiful lakes, rivers, and mountains. Greenville is 2½ hours from Atlanta, 1½ hours from Charlotte, and only one hour from Asheville, North Carolina. Greenville is within easy reach of the Blue Ridge Mountains and Atlantic Beaches. The newly renovated Greenville-Spartanburg Airport, located just 25 minutes from downtown, runs daily flights to major cities and airline hubs. It is an ideal place to live and work. Applicants should submit the following documents as a single PDF in the order listed: a letter of interest, C.V., statement of teaching philosophy and evidence of teaching effectiveness, a statement of scholarly interests, representative publications, and complete contact information for three references. The statement of teaching philosophy should describe your inclusive teaching and mentoring efforts, broadly conceived, and how your teaching and mentoring may contribute to a liberal arts and sciences community that aims, among other things, to “honor inquiry, promote diversity, [and] strive for equity” ( FUture Focused ). You may also discuss any relevant professional development, service contributions, or other experiences that have refined your skills or demonstrate your efforts in these areas. Selected candidates will be asked to arrange for 3 letters of recommendation to be submitted. Questions about the position can be sent to Dr. Erin Hahn, Department Chair ( erin.hahn@furman.edu ).   Review of applications begins September 25, 2026. Education Requirements: Certification Requirements: Job Posting End Date (if date is blank, posting is open ended):"
    },
